-- title:
--   Second degeneracy leg equals first composed with Atkin–Lehner
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $K$ a field of characteristic $p$ with decidable equality, and $M,s$ nonzero natural numbers. Let $X$ be a supersingular level datum `SSLevelDatum p K M s`; among its data are the membership facts $j(q^M),j(q^s)\in F_{Ms}$, where $F_N\subseteq K(\!(q)\!)$ denotes the $K$-subfield of Laurent series generated by $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$, the integrality of the inclusion $\alpha=$ `levelAlphaC` $: F_M\to F_{Ms}$ and of the $s$-th substitution $\beta=$ `levelBetaC` $: F_M\to F_{Ms}$ (induced by $q\mapsto q^s$ on Laurent series), a $K$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $F_{Ms}$ satisfying the Atkin–Lehner relations $\sigma(j(q))=j(q^s)$, $\sigma(j(q^s))=j(q)$, $\sigma(j(q^{Ms}))=j(q^M)$, $\sigma(j(q^M))=j(q^{Ms})$, together with the facts that restriction along $\alpha$ and along $\beta$ carry supersingular places of level $Ms$ to supersingular places of level $M$ and that the supersingular places of level $Ms$ are stable under the induced permutation of places. For every supersingular place $W$ of $F_{Ms}$ (a valuation subring satisfying `IsSupersingularPlace p (M*s) K`), the assertion is that the restriction of $W$ along $\beta$ coincides, as a place of $F_M$, with the restriction along $\alpha$ of the place obtained from $W$ by transport along $\sigma$; that is, `X.snd W = X.fst (X.atkinLehnerPerm W)`.
--
--   This is the standard compatibility of the two degeneracy maps $X_0(Ms)\to X_0(M)$ with the Atkin–Lehner involution $w_s$, here on the level of supersingular places of the modular function fields in characteristic $p$; it allows statements about one leg to be read off from the other. It is used in the analysis of the supersingular isogeny graph feeding into the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, specifically by [`CerednikDrinfeld.classSet_eq_empty_or_eq_univ_of_forall_mem_iff_of_squarefree`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.classSet_eq_empty_or_eq_univ_of_forall_mem_iff_of_squarefree).
